# The command line fits its measurements and says how it went. `fit` makes the sum `Fit | Failed` in one of two arms
# (its early return is the one arm, what follows the other), and one copairing takes it apart where it arises:
# `describe` matches it and builds a Report in either arm, which the command line prints.

route fits.cli.main
step main/for x in sys.argv[1:]                                    # each word the human typed, kept as `x`
step main/fit
choice main/fit/?1
step main/fit/?1/Failed()
step main/fit/?1/Fit()                                  # what follows the early return is the other arm
step main/describe
choice main/describe/?1
step main/describe/?1/Report()
step main/describe/?1/Report()#2

line entry > main call
line entry > main/for x in sys.argv[1:] call                       # the command line is the entry's
line main/for x in sys.argv[1:] > _·x@main/for x in sys.argv[1:] value
line _·x@main/for x in sys.argv[1:] > main/fit value               # `fit([float(x) for x in ..])`
line main/fit/?1/Failed() > Failed@main/fit/?1 value   # with Fit() in the other arm, the sum either arm makes
line main/fit/?1/Fit() > Fit@main/fit/?1 value
line Failed@main/fit/?1 > main/fit value                           # fit hands back what either arm made
line Fit@main/fit/?1 > main/fit value
line main/fit > Fit | Failed@main/fit value                        # fit gives one value, the sum
known #126 line Fit | Failed@main/fit > main/describe value        # the match in describe's own body opens it
line Fit | Failed@main/fit > main/describe/?1/Report() value         # `case Fit(score=s)`: `s` is a part of the sum
line Fit | Failed@main/fit > main/describe/?1/Report()#2 value       # `case Failed(reason=why)`
line main/describe/?1/Report() > Report@main/describe/?1 value
line main/describe/?1/Report()#2 > Report@main/describe/?1 value
line Report@main/describe/?1 > main/describe value
line main/describe > Report·report@main/describe value
known #101 line Report·report@main/describe > main value            # main prints the line and the points
line main > Screen own

home Failed@main/fit/?1 main/fit
home Fit@main/fit/?1 main/fit
home _·x@main/for x in sys.argv[1:] main
home Fit | Failed@main/fit main
home Report@main/describe/?1 main/describe
home Report·report@main/describe main

side entry left
side Screen right
